# Implementation Coding Standards

- Keep modules plug-and-play with explicit interfaces and dependency injection.
- Do not couple core orchestration to UI, API transport, or provider-specific SDK internals.
- Keep provider SDK imports isolated to adapter modules; core layers must consume only internal runtime contracts.
- Treat model tool calls as intent; route state-changing side effects through deterministic tool execution and policy gates.
- Prefer composition over inheritance for runtime adapters, tools, and policies.
- Require a top-of-file docstring/header that documents file path, role, and key file relations.
- Every state-changing operation must include validation, policy checks, and structured logs.
- Require typed schemas for inter-module inputs/outputs and error envelopes.
- Include tests for happy path, failure path, and retry/timeout behavior.
- Keep changes incremental; avoid big-bang rewrites unless explicitly approved.
- Keep code simple (KISS) and event-oriented where orchestration benefits from decoupling.
